    "title": "pandas.DatetimeIndex.to_period — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeIndex.to_period#\n\n- \nDatetimeIndex.to_period(*freq=None* )[source]#\n- Cast to PeriodArray/PeriodIndex at a particular frequency. Converts DatetimeArray/Index to PeriodArray/PeriodIndex. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **freq** str, optional\n    - One of pandas’ period aliases. Will be inferred by default.\n  - Returns:\n    - PeriodArray/PeriodIndex\n    - Immutable ndarray holding ordinal values at a particular frequency.\n  - Raises:\n    - ValueError\n    - When converting a DatetimeArray/Index with non-regular values, so that a frequency cannot be inferred.\n See also \n  - `PeriodIndex`\n  - Immutable ndarray holding ordinal values.\n  - `DatetimeIndex.to_pydatetime`\n  - Return DatetimeIndex as object.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame( ... {\"y\": [1, 2, 3]}, ... index=pd.to_datetime( ... [ ... \"2000-03-31 00:00:00\", ... \"2000-05-31 00:00:00\", ... \"2000-08-31 00:00:00\", ... ] ... ), ... ) >>> df.index.to_period(\"M\") PeriodIndex(['2000-03', '2000-05', '2000-08'], dtype='period[M]') Infer the daily frequency >>> idx = pd.date_range(\"2017-01-01\", periods=2) >>> idx.to_period() PeriodIndex(['2017-01-01', '2017-01-02'], dtype='period[D]')",
    "markdown_length": 1151,
